---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import BuiltByDevin from '../components/BuiltByDevin.astro';
import { stats } from '../lib/prs';

const s = stats();
---
<Base title="About" description="What this site is and how the numbers in it were produced.">
  <h1>About</h1>
  <p>
    <BuiltByDevin />
  </p>
  <p>
    Most of discover-feed was built through Devin sessions; this site tells that
    story — see the <a href="/timeline">timeline</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    This is the build log of
    <a href="https://github.com/babcoccl/discover-feed" rel="noopener">discover-feed</a>,
    a personal "Discover-style" news reader: profiles with topics and sources, RSS/Atom
    and API ingestion, article clustering into stories, LLM-written briefs and reports,
    web-search enrichment, alerts, and a public API. The stack is Python 3.12, FastAPI,
    SQLAlchemy + SQLite, APScheduler, Jinja2 + HTMX + Tailwind, with a local
    OpenAI-compatible LLM (Qwen3.5 9B on llama.cpp).
  </p>
  <p>
    Almost the entire application was written by Devin, a coding agent, across
    {s.total} pull requests over {s.days} days — {s.merged} merged for
    +{s.additions.toLocaleString('en-US')} / −{s.deletions.toLocaleString('en-US')} lines.
    Each session was driven by a written spec: a context paragraph, numbered tasks,
    acceptance criteria and non-goals, ending with "open a PR and stop."
  </p>
  <p>
    This site is itself a Devin session's output: Astro, static output, generated
    timeline from the repository's PR metadata, hosted on Cloudflare Pages. Everything
    stated in a post traces to a merged PR (linked by number), a file in the repo, or
    the author's explicit notes. Nothing here publishes session transcripts, private
    addresses, or credentials — a leak scan runs in CI on every change to
    <code>blog/</code>.
  </p>
  <p>
    Tone on purpose: candid engineering log, not marketing. Where something failed,
    the post says so and cites the fix.
  </p>
</Base>
